[{:db/id "af165af8-ee5a-57c7-a376-9cddd1c42513" :answer/id #uuid "af165af8-ee5a-57c7-a376-9cddd1c42513" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10 \\sqrt{70}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "52b8d8e7-0592-5b58-8e87-3aef78c72a94" :answer/id #uuid "52b8d8e7-0592-5b58-8e87-3aef78c72a94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "100" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "48231604-0e12-5a6d-a30d-1c9f42fc155f" :answer/id #uuid "48231604-0e12-5a6d-a30d-1c9f42fc155f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5 \\sqrt{30}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "aa3c8f9f-076f-5a93-a3e7-2bef1961bd4b" :answer/id #uuid "aa3c8f9f-076f-5a93-a3e7-2bef1961bd4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "50" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "693f9a8b-9776-594c-ab46-cfd34df427e3" :answer/id #uuid "693f9a8b-9776-594c-ab46-cfd34df427e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5 \\sqrt{35}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "598cd05f-a758-55c1-9174-123016a1cdf8" :answer-field/id #uuid "598cd05f-a758-55c1-9174-123016a1cdf8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["af165af8-ee5a-57c7-a376-9cddd1c42513" "52b8d8e7-0592-5b58-8e87-3aef78c72a94" "48231604-0e12-5a6d-a30d-1c9f42fc155f" "aa3c8f9f-076f-5a93-a3e7-2bef1961bd4b" "693f9a8b-9776-594c-ab46-cfd34df427e3"] :answer-field/correct "af165af8-ee5a-57c7-a376-9cddd1c42513" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "0f95e766-a2a3-5446-8a69-b8c1d5e53063" :question/id #uuid "0f95e766-a2a3-5446-8a69-b8c1d5e53063" :question/problem "Find the surface area of the parametric surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=2u-v,\\,y=3u+2,\\,z=u+2v\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 5$ and $-1\\le v\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2u-v,\\,3u+2,\\,u+2v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3u+2),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,3,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3u+2),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,0,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,\\,-5,\\,3⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨6,\\,-5,\\,3⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+(-5)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36+25+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{70}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, let's denote\n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 5,\\,-1\\le v\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nThen, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{70}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{70}{∬}_{D}\\text{ }\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{70}\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{70}\\cdot 5\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =10 \\sqrt{70}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["598cd05f-a758-55c1-9174-123016a1cdf8"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "7c8f8746-3757-5c4f-81cf-138acecbfbba" :answer/id #uuid "7c8f8746-3757-5c4f-81cf-138acecbfbba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10 \\sqrt{57} \\pi" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "f066d9dd-0037-5da1-9b02-de938feb9f43" :answer/id #uuid "f066d9dd-0037-5da1-9b02-de938feb9f43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5 \\sqrt{19} \\pi" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "8a470d9a-3f5a-5616-9e52-a8ba1ef520a1" :answer/id #uuid "8a470d9a-3f5a-5616-9e52-a8ba1ef520a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20 \\sqrt{19} \\pi" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "362d1394-b2a3-59f8-a7c6-b46fc08ba352" :answer/id #uuid "362d1394-b2a3-59f8-a7c6-b46fc08ba352" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5 \\sqrt{38} \\pi" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "8934de87-c2a8-50dc-a859-18d9952684f6" :answer/id #uuid "8934de87-c2a8-50dc-a859-18d9952684f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10 \\sqrt{38} \\pi" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "f72f9232-4b2e-53c4-9085-4f50862a7a79" :answer-field/id #uuid "f72f9232-4b2e-53c4-9085-4f50862a7a79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["7c8f8746-3757-5c4f-81cf-138acecbfbba" "f066d9dd-0037-5da1-9b02-de938feb9f43" "8a470d9a-3f5a-5616-9e52-a8ba1ef520a1" "362d1394-b2a3-59f8-a7c6-b46fc08ba352" "8934de87-c2a8-50dc-a859-18d9952684f6"] :answer-field/correct "8a470d9a-3f5a-5616-9e52-a8ba1ef520a1" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "e42dd0ba-94bb-571f-b81d-083720a4e84b" :question/id #uuid "e42dd0ba-94bb-571f-b81d-083720a4e84b" :question/problem "Find the surface area of the part of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=⟨-u+v,\\,u-2v,\\,3v⟩$ that is subject to the constraint ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 20.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-2,\\,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,3,\\,1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨3,\\,3,\\,1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+9+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that the region ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 20$ corresponds to the disk\n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 20},\n$$\n\nof radius $2 \\sqrt{5}.$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{19}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{19}{∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{19}\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{19}\\cdot (\\pi \\cdot (2 \\sqrt{5})^{2}) \\\\  & =20 \\sqrt{19} \\pi.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["f72f9232-4b2e-53c4-9085-4f50862a7a79"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "generator" :question-generator/id #uuid "92f3e1ca-f67b-5933-9d82-67166ccbf4d0" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186119888.py"} [:db/add 17592186119888 :knowledge-point/question-generator "generator"] {:db/id 17592186119888 :knowledge-point/questions ["0f95e766-a2a3-5446-8a69-b8c1d5e53063" "e42dd0ba-94bb-571f-b81d-083720a4e84b"]} [:db/ensure 17592186119888 :knowledge-point/validate]]
